The first statement changes the error handling to immediately jump to fallback logic when `ENOSYS` is encountered, preventing the incorrect propagation of this error. The second statement initializes `mount_id` and `mount_id_parent` to `-1`, ensuring that they have a defined value before any comparisons are made, thus avoiding undefined behavior when comparing these variables.


